 "limits": [
  "float32 and float16 use the Metal kernels; float64, bfloat16 and every non-MPS device run the conv1d composition, which is exact but not the fast path.",
  "causal_conv1d_update is the decode path and carries no autograd; it raises when x, weight or state requires grad.",
  "the state of causal_conv1d_update must have stride 1 in its last dimension: a slice of a larger cache is fine because the kernel reads the strides, a transpose is not, because the buffer is written in place.",
  "seq_idx (sequence-boundary masks for packed batches) is not implemented.",
  "the tap count is a compile-time constant in the Metal sources, so a new K compiles one shader the first time it is used.",
  "a row length that is not a multiple of four (eight for the fp16 forward) drops to one element per thread: correct, and slower by the loads it then issues one at a time.",
  "fp16 accumulates the taps and the bias in float32 and rounds once; values agree with the float64 reference to about 2e-4 relative, not bit-exactly."
